  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Freezing point depression refers to the lowering of the freezing point of solvent&nbsp;upon the addition of solute.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>88</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.27</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
